# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# NION Orchestration Engine — Environment Configuration Template
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# INSTRUCTIONS
# ─────────────
# 1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your API key below (replace the placeholder value).
# 3. Never commit .env to version control — it is listed in .gitignore.
#
# Get a free NVIDIA NIM API key at: https://build.nvidia.com
#   • Click any model  →  "Get API Key"
#   • Keys are prefixed: nvapi-
#   • No credit card required for the free tier
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── PRIMARY: NVIDIA NIM (default, recommended) ────────────────────────────────
#
# LLM_PROVIDER controls which inference backend the engine uses.
# Valid values: nvidia | openai | gemini
#
LLM_PROVIDER=nvidia

# Your NVIDIA NIM API key.
# Replace the placeholder below with your actual key.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Model to use for all LLM calls.
# The default below is recommended for structured JSON output tasks.
# See README §4 for alternative model options.
NVIDIA_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct


# ── ALTERNATIVE: OpenAI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# To switch to OpenAI, set LLM_PROVIDER=openai and provide your key.
# Comment out the NVIDIA section above before uncommenting these lines.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini


# ── ALTERNATIVE: Google Gemini ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# To switch to Gemini, set LLM_PROVIDER=gemini and provide your key.
# Requires: pip install langchain-google-genai
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIzaxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
